<title>CHINA: China Chiwan Petroleum to issue dividend.</title>
<headline>China Chiwan Petroleum to issue dividend.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's Shenzhen Chiwan Petroleum Supply Base Co Ltd said on Friday it would make a US$0.02 cash dividend per share based on 1996 profits.</p>
<p>The registration deadline was July 24 and the firm's B shares would go ex-dividend on July 22, the Shenzhen-listed company said in a statement in the Shenzhen-based Securities Times.</p>
<p>Holders of the company's B shares could receive their dividend in Hong Kong dollars at an exchange rate of US$1 to HK$7.7375, from July 25, it said.</p>
<p>(US$1=8.3 yuan US$1=HK$7.8)</p>
</text>
